rings and seals in funerary contexts with case studies from Sellopoulo, Vapheio,
and Pylos. Instead, this thesis proposes that assemblages of multiple signet 
rings and sealstones in funerary contexts are the result of the ritualized 
bestowal of these objects by relatives, dependents, and close associates of the 
