      "local_ref": "d2",
      "document_summary": "Theodore Eliopoulos’s article “Some observations on 
the iconography of the ‘Ring of Nestor’”, published in 2013 in the refereed 
journal Annuario della Scuola Archeologica di Atene e delle Missioni Italiane in
Oriente, offers a detailed re-examination of the iconography of the Ring of 
Nestor. The study discusses the individual visual motifs on the ring, reassesses
earlier interpretations such as Evans’s reading of an after-world scene, and 
engages with alternative readings including epiphany, funerary, and mythological
interpretations. Eliopoulos reviews prior scholarship and places the ring within
wider debates on Aegean glyptic imagery, focusing particularly on the role of 
incurved altars and related iconographic elements. The article also addresses 
authenticity questions, situating the Ring of Nestor in discussions of forgeries
and evaluating evidence for and against its genuineness through iconographic 
comparison with securely provenanced pieces. Methodologically, the paper 
emphasizes iconographic analysis and historiography to refine understanding of 
the ring’s imagery and significance.",
