"importance": "core"}, "items": [{"id": "20260628160517905794_93d573cc", "type":
"Evidence", "text": "The Heidelberg digital library entry for Evans’s work lists
the title as \"Evans, Arthur J.: 'The ring of Nestor'. A glimpse into the Minoan
after-world and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia\" and assigns it the DOI https://doi.org/10.11588/diglit.808.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628160356958135_b804fece"], "citations": [19]}, {"id": 
"20260628160517984434_db798573", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Heidelberg 
record notes that Evans’s monograph has 75 pages and includes sections titled 
\"A sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, 
Boeotia\" and \"A glimpse into the Minoan after-world.\"", "source_ids": 
["20260628160356958135_b804fece"], "citations": [19]}, {"id": 
"20260628160518054253_d9b53cfd", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Academia.edu 
metadata for Eliopoulos’s article identifies the title as \"SOME OBSERVATIONS ON
THE ICONOGRAPHY OF THE 'RING OF NESTOR'\", lists the venue as \"ANNUARIO della 
Scuola Archeologica di Atene e delle Missioni Italiane in Oriente\", and gives 
the year as 2013.", "source_ids": ["20260628155934886510_6c8b75ae"], 
"citations": [2]}, {"id": "20260628160518128879_0b86045e", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The description of Eliopoulos’s article states that it is a 22-page 
study focusing on iconographic analysis of the Ring of Nestor and engaging with 
issues of authenticity and forgery within Aegean glyptic.", "source_ids": 
["20260628155934886510_6c8b75ae"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628160518209236_2a894e4b", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The KU 
ScholarWorks PDF of \"Current Approaches and New Perspectives in Aegean 
Iconography\" includes a reference to \"Evans 1925. A. J. Evans, 'The Ring of 
Nestor': A Glimpse into the Minoan After-World and a Sepulchral Treasure of Gold
Signet-Rings and Bead ...\" in its list of cited literature.", "source_ids": 
["20260628155959507467_19b3d46f"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260628160518283299_a0090745", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The HathiTrust 
catalog entry records the title as \"ʻThe ring of Nestor;̓ a glimpse into the 
Minoan after-world, and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia\" and lists Sir Arthur Evans as the author with 
a publication date of 1925.", "source_ids": ["20260628160516218905_aecfba47"], 
"citations": [20]}, {"id": "20260628160518365351_f68b9d2d", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The National Library of Ireland catalogue entry for \"The ring of 
Nestor\" gives the full title as \"The ring of Nestor: a glimpse into the Minoan
after-world, and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia\" and attributes it to Sir Arthur Evans.", "source_ids": 
["20260628160516251204_0425faa7"], "citations": [21]}, {"id": 
"20260628160518449104_6a00665e", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Texas 
ScholarWorks repository entry describes the thesis \"Multiple signet rings and 
seals in Bronze Age Aegean funerary contexts: objects as embodiment and ritual 
traces\" as examining multiple signet rings and seals in funerary contexts at 
sites including Sellopoulo, Vapheio, and Pylos, and notes that it is housed at 
the University of Texas at Austin.", "source_ids": 
["20260628160516285899_03a8e18a"], "citations": [22]}, {"id": 
"20260628160518538957_7ad1ff4f", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The thesis 
abstract states that the study approaches signet rings and seals as objects of 
embodiment and ritual traces within Bronze Age Aegean funerary practices, 
emphasizing methodological questions about interpreting such assemblages.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628160516285899_03a8e18a"], "citations": [22]}, {"id": 
"20260628160545548056_03c2e0e2", "type": "Claim", "text": "Arthur J. Evans’s 
1925 monograph \"The ring of Nestor: a glimpse into the Minoan after-world, and 
a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia\"
is a stand‑alone scholarly study published by Macmillan that describes and 
interprets a gold signet ring known as the \"Ring of Nestor\" within a Late 
Bronze Age, Minoan‑influenced Mycenaean funerary context.", "source_ids": 
["20260628160356958135_b804fece", "20260628160516218905_aecfba47", 
"20260628160516251204_0425faa7"], "citations": [19, 20, 21]}, {"id": 
"20260628160545895564_fb0bbbd3", "type": "Claim", "text": "Evans structures his 
1925 study of the Ring of Nestor into a descriptive section on the Thisbê gold 
signet rings and bead seals and a second section that interprets the Ring of 
Nestor’s multi‑figure scene as a glimpse into a Minoan after‑world, emphasizing 
altars, deities, and afterlife‑related religious imagery.", "source_ids": 
["20260628160356958135_b804fece"], "citations": [19]}, {"id": 
"20260628160546007873_952b7ed7", "type": "Claim", "text": "Evans’s 1925 
monograph on the Ring of Nestor is securely attested in multiple scholarly 
catalogues (HathiTrust, Heidelberg Digital Library, National Library of 
Ireland), which agree on its authorship by Sir Arthur Evans, its 1925 
publication date, and its full title, and the Heidelberg digital copy carries 
the DOI 10.11588/diglit.808.", "source_ids": ["20260628160356958135_b804fece", 
"20260628160516218905_aecfba47", "20260628160516251204_0425faa7"], "citations": 
[19, 20, 21]}, {"id": "20260628160546220596_322ccad0", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"Theodore Eliopoulos’s 2013 article \"Some observations on the iconography of 
the 'Ring of Nestor'\" in the refereed journal \"Annuario della Scuola 
Archeologica di Atene e delle Missioni Italiane in Oriente\" offers a 22‑page 
iconographic re‑analysis of the Ring of Nestor, reassessing Evans’s after‑world 
interpretation and engaging with debates on the ring’s authenticity and possible
forgery.", "source_ids": ["20260628155934886510_6c8b75ae"], "citations": [2]}, 
{"id": "20260628160546450198_5d4d2635", "type": "Claim", "text": "Eliopoulos’s 
study of the Ring of Nestor highlights incurved altars and related iconographic 
elements on the ring as crucial for evaluating both prior interpretive models 
(such as epiphany, funerary, or mythological readings) and the question of the 
ring’s authenticity within broader discussions of Aegean glyptic forgeries.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628155934886510_6c8b75ae"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628160546592858_2d3f4b90", "type": "Claim", "text": "The volume \"Current 
Approaches and New Perspectives in Aegean Iconography\" includes peer‑reviewed 
chapters that cite Evans’s 1925 study of the Ring of Nestor and use it as a case
study in discussions of Aegean iconography, particularly miniature sacred 
landscapes and ritual scenes on Minoan or Minoanizing gold rings, thereby 
revisiting his interpretations and dating.", "source_ids": 
["20260628155959507467_19b3d46f"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260628160546720165_762bb730", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Texas 
ScholarWorks thesis \"Multiple signet rings and seals in Bronze Age Aegean 
funerary contexts: objects as embodiment and ritual traces\" examines 
assemblages of signet rings and seals from sites including Sellopoulo, Vapheio, 
and Pylos, using a material‑anthropological approach that foregrounds 
methodological issues in interpreting funerary ring assemblages as embodiments 
of persons and ritual traces.", "source_ids": ["20260628160516285899_03a8e18a"],
"citations": [22]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 50, "total": 16, "next_offset": null}
