   Ring of Nestor should be regarded as an authentic Late Bronze Age ring       
   participating in the same Minoanizing Mycenaean iconographic koine as the    
   Griffin Warrior rings, arguing that a modern forger could not have           
   anticipated the patterns observed in the newly excavated grave. [14]         
